From f0660e3bc98588a534d75298008e732b128e0d97 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: c4ffein <c4ffein.work@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 4 Jul 2026 23:18:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Bugfix: pair terminal vertices with their own domain when
 building `deco 0` architectures

The terminal vertex array built by archDecoArchBuild() must associate,
for each terminal vertex, its label with the terminal number of the
domain which contains THAT vertex in the recursive bipartition.

The pre-e6c094fc code read `mapDomain (&mappdat, tgtvertnum - baseval)`;
since mappdat.parttax is rebased at initialization time, the base was
subtracted twice: base-1 graphs read parttax[-1] (out-of-bounds) for
their first vertex and the domain of the wrong vertex for all others.

Commit e6c094fc replaced the lookup with `&mappdat.domntab[termdomnum]`,
which assumes that domain index i is the domain of terminal vertex i.
This does not hold: domain indices are assigned in job-splitting order
(driven by a LIFO job list), not in vertex order.  As soon as both
halves of a bipartition need further splitting, labels are attached to
the wrong leaves of the decomposition tree, at any base value.
Minimal counterexample: a 4-vertex weighted path whose edge loads force
the bipartition sequence {0,1}|{2,3}, then {0}|{1}, then {2}|{3};
vertices 1 and 2 end up swapped in the decomposition tree, so sibling
leaves carry labels {0,2} instead of {0,1}.  The resulting architecture
is internally consistent but its tree no longer reflects the topology
of the input graph, silently degrading the quality of every mapping
computed onto it.

The proper fix is to keep the parttax lookup and drop only the spurious
rebasing, as parttax is already a based array: this is also how every
other mapDomain() call site passes vertex indices.
---
 src/libscotch/arch_build.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/libscotch/arch_build.c b/src/libscotch/arch_build.c
index 97cf98c..a369de8 100644
--- a/src/libscotch/arch_build.c
+++ b/src/libscotch/arch_build.c
@@ -306,7 +306,7 @@ Context * const             contptr)              /*+ Execution context
     tgtvertnum = (tgtlistptr != NULL) ? tgtlistptr->vnumtab[termdomnum] : (termdomnum + tgtgrafptr->baseval);
     termverttab[termdomnum].labl = tgtvertnum;
     termverttab[termdomnum].wght = (tgtgrafptr->velotax != NULL) ? tgtgrafptr->velotax[tgtvertnum] : 1;
-    termverttab[termdomnum].num  = archDomNum (&archdat, &mappdat.domntab[termdomnum]);
+    termverttab[termdomnum].num  = archDomNum (&archdat, mapDomain (&mappdat, tgtvertnum));
     if (termverttab[termdomnum].num > termdommax) /* Find maximum terminal number */
       termdommax = termverttab[termdomnum].num;
   }
